: What are matter waves? State De-Broglie hypothesis.":[81,83],"#Questions and Answers##CL7_Q1: What are matter waves? State De-Broglie hypothesis.#{1}":[82,83],"#Questions and Answers##CL7_Q2: Why is the wave nature of matter not apparent for macroscopic particles?":[84,86],"#Questions and Answers##CL7_Q2: Why is the wave nature of matter not apparent for macroscopic particles?#{1}":[85,86],"#Questions and Answers##CL7_Q3: Calculate the de-Broglie wavelength of an oxygen molecule with mass $5.4\\times10^{-26}$ kg moving at 500 m/s.":[87,91],"#Questions and Answers##CL7_Q3: Calculate the de-Broglie wavelength of an oxygen molecule with mass $5.4\\times10^{-26}$ kg moving at 500 m/s.#{1}":[88,91],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q1: The Uncertainty principle is not significant in the case of macro-bodies. Justify.":[92,96],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q1: The Uncertainty principle is not significant in the case of macro-bodies. Justify.#{1}":[93,96],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q2: A shutter opens for $\\Delta t = 10^{-10}$ s. What is the spread in frequency of the light that passes through?":[97,101],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q2: A shutter opens for $\\Delta t = 10^{-10}$ s. What is the spread in frequency of the light that passes through?#{1}":[98,101],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q3: An electron and a 150g baseball are travelling at 220 m/s with 0.065% accuracy. Compare the uncertainty in their positions.":[102,111],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q3: An electron and a 150g baseball are travelling at 220 m/s with 0.065% accuracy. Compare the uncertainty in their positions.#{1}":[103,103],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q3: An electron and a 150g baseball are travelling at 220 m/s with 0.065% accuracy. Compare the uncertainty in their positions.#{2}":[104,104],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q3: An electron and a 150g baseball are travelling at 220 m/s with 0.065% accuracy. Compare the uncertainty in their positions.#{3}":[105,105],"#Questions and Answers##CL8_Q3: An electro