0 < x < L$.#{1}":[137,137],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{2}":[138,138],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{3}":[139,139],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{4}":[140,140],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{5}":[141,141],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{6}":[142,143],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{7}":[144,145],"#Questions and Answers##CL12_Q2: Normalize the wave function $\\psi = A \\sin(\\frac{\\pi x}{L})$ for $0 < x < L$.#{8}":[146,147],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q1: Explain the concept of \"expectation value\".":[148,151],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q1: Explain the concept of \"expectation value\".#{1}":[149,151],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q2: Explain operators and observables.":[152,155],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q2: Explain operators and observables.#{1}":[153,153],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q2: Explain operators and observables.#{2}":[154,155],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q3: Find the expectation value of position, $\\langle x \\rangle$, for a particle in a box of width L.":[156,161],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q3: Find the expectation value of position, $\\langle x \\rangle$, for a particle in a box of width L.#{1}":[157,161],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q4: Describe an Eigen value equation.":[162,168],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q4: Describe an Eigen value equation.#{1}":[163,164],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q4: Describe an Eigen value equation.#{2}":[165,165],"#Questions and Answers##CL14_Q4: Describe an Eigen value equation.#{3}":[166,166],"#